      },
      "lineNbr": 506,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-12T15:57:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It doesn\u0027t hold an instance, it uses a raw pointer: `ModuleConfig* mModuleConfig`. Holding a raw pointer does not affect the lifetime of an object, even if somewhere else a smart pointer is used. Would we actually need to hold an instance, we would use a `shared_ptr` in `WithDevicePortConnectedState`.\n\nHowever, the instance of `ModuleConfig` is owned by the test, thus it\u0027s OK to use a raw pointer in `WithDevicePortConnectedState`. That\u0027s why we can keep using `unique_ptr` here, as the test is the sole owner for `ModuleConfig`.\n\nAs a side note, we always use `shared_ptr` for instances of AIDL interfaces (for example, `std::shared_ptr\u003cIModule\u003e`), that\u0027s because they are intended to be held by multiple instances. However, for simple cases it\u0027s preferred to use a simpler `unique_ptr`.",
      "parentUuid": "0811c902_46f443e4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 506,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 506,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "6801be153087571e54a0cb03de195d91d6f6f089",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
