      "writtenOn": "2023-09-11T17:18:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using `GTEST_SKIP` in a function will not make the test to exit early. `GTEST_SKIP` can only abort the current function: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/googletest/googletest/include/gtest/gtest.h;l\u003d1887;drc\u003d050b51751840837e9da6dad684c5ae0f87ab1f60. Since skipping a test does not generate a fatal failure (skipping is neither a failure nor a success), `ASSERT_NO_FATAL_FAILURE` will not react to it.\n\nWhat I would suggest is to add a boolean flag field to `WithRemoteSubmix` class which needs to be set to true if the test has to be skipped. Then the test needs to check that flag after doing the setup and use `GTEST_SKIP` at the level of the test function, where it should work properly.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4070,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4070,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "6801be153087571e54a0cb03de195d91d6f6f089",
